+// COGBox SDK patch 106 (GitHub #329): a Gears 3 save set signed with a key COGBox can't name (an earlier online account
+// after a new one was made, a save from another PC or console, an old backup put back) used to be left alone, and Gears 3
+// then reset it and wrote fresh files over it - the progress was gone.
+//
+// CogAdoptSaveFiles re-signs one set for to_key without knowing its old key (the data is never changed, only the
+// 20-byte signature), but only a whole, plausible save: PlayerStorage.dat alone (4 KB - 64 KB, not all zero), or the
+// full profile set 63E83FFF + 63E83FFE + 63E83FFD (each at most 1000 bytes; 63E83FFF holding data, FFE / FFD empty or
+// not all zero - Gears 3 writes FFD empty; the three written within an hour of each other, as the game writes them
+// together); every file readable (Refused / ReadFailed otherwise, nothing written). files[0] is first copied to
+// <file>.cogbox-adopted-<stamp> (a new name each time, never replacing anything), then written through
+// <file>.cogbox-tmp and renamed over the original. AlreadyDone when the set is signed for to_key already.
+ResignResult CogAdoptSaveFiles(const std::vector<std::filesystem::path>& files, uint64_t to_key);
+// Every Gears 3 save set under user_data_root not signed for run_key is adopted as above. Each adoption is noted in
+// <user_data_root>/cogbox-save-adopted; for the same run_key, a noted body found signed with another key again is left
+// alone unless it carries its pre-adoption signature again (the player put that file back), and a save adopted 3 times
+// already is left alone (the game signs with a key COGBox doesn't predict - no loop of copies). Never throws.
+void CogAdoptGears3Saves(const std::filesystem::path& user_data_root, uint64_t profile_xuid, uint64_t run_key);
+// The keys recent runs signed their saves with (<user_data_root>/cogbox-save-key: one 16-hex-digit key a line, newest
+// first, at most 8; any other line is ignored), and the newest of them.
+std::vector<uint64_t> CogSaveKeyHistory(const std::filesystem::path& user_data_root);
+std::optional<uint64_t> CogLastSaveKey(const std::filesystem::path& user_data_root);
+// run_key becomes the newest key of that history (written atomically). False if it couldn't be written.
+bool CogNoteSaveKey(const std::filesystem::path& user_data_root, uint64_t run_key);
+// When run_key differs from the last run's (none noted counts as a change), every Gears 3 / Judgment save file in place
+// (PlayerStorage.dat, Judgment's header, the profile settings 63E83FFF/E/D and players 2-4's .p2 - .p4) is copied to
+// <user_data_root>/_cogbox-save-backups/<nnnnnn>-<stamp>-<old key|first|unknown>-to-<new key>/ under the same relative
+// path (nnnnnn a sequence number; built in a .cogbox-tmp folder and renamed when whole). Afterwards, while more than 20
+// copies are there, a copy whose saves are all also in a newer copy (same data; a signature may differ) is removed,
+// oldest first - never the oldest copy, a "first" one, the one just made, or any folder not named as above. The key is
+// NOT noted here (CogNoteSaveKey, once the start-up passes are done). A file that can't be read fails the copy (no
+// folder left). NotApplicable for a user folder of another game (no Gears 3 / Judgment folder). Never throws.
+enum class SnapshotResult { NotApplicable, NotNeeded, Copied, Failed };
+SnapshotResult CogSnapshotSavesOnKeyChange(const std::filesystem::path& user_data_root, uint64_t profile_xuid,
+                                           uint64_t run_key);
+// Everything done to the Gears 3 saves at start-up, in order: the copy above; the verified conversions from other_key,
+// from each key of the history and from extra_key (--cogbox_save_adopt_key) to run_key; only then, if adopt_foreign,
+// the unverified adoption; the per-set verdict (CogReportGears3SaveSigning); and last, if the copy was made or not
+// needed, run_key noted. other_key == run_key: no conversion from it.
+void CogPrepareGears3Saves(const std::filesystem::path& user_data_root, uint64_t profile_xuid, uint64_t run_key,
+                           uint64_t other_key, bool adopt_foreign, std::optional<uint64_t> extra_key);
+
 // Judgment ties PlayerStorage.dat and its profile settings to the sign-in (LIVE or local) in a way we can't re-sign, so
 // switching online play on or off made the game start them fresh. Instead each mode keeps its own copy: on a switch,
 // the files of the mode being left are moved aside as <file>.cogbox-<mode>, and the other mode's copies come back.
